[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/comments/6714769340","html_url":"https://github.com/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/240#issuecomment-6714769340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/240","id":6714769340,"node_id":"IC_kwDORR9opc8AAAABkDs_vA","user":{"login":"kenneives","id":101359438,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgqfTg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101359438?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives","html_url":"https://github.com/kenneives","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenneives/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T00:00:33Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T00:00:33Z","body":"Thank you for this. A separate read of the live server reproducing all three signed digests is a stronger check than a run against our pinned file, because it shows the derivation holds outside our own fixtures.\n\nIt's also useful that your implementation was written from the README alone. That's what the README is for.\n\nWould you be OK with us linking this from the v1 README as an outside read of the server? I'd like to read your notes on what makes two readers disagree, too. Pagination and launch environment are the cases I'd most like to get right.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/comments/6714769340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/comments/6775034881","html_url":"https://github.com/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/240#issuecomment-6775034881","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/240","id":6775034881,"node_id":"IC_kwDORR9opc8AAAABk9LUAQ","user":{"login":"alexar76","id":86793359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NzkzMzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86793359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76","html_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexar76/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-10T17:58:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T17:58:32Z","body":"Yes, please link it, and thank you.\n\nWhat made two readers disagree, from our comparison with heldfast on 31 October\n([README](https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/interop-digests-2026-10-31/README.md), \"Checks behind the rows\")\nand a check against rugsnare on 26 October:\n\n**Pagination.** heldfast sends one `tools/list` with no cursor. On 11 servers HISTOR read more than one page. Read live on 31 October, 10 of them served a first page of exactly heldfast's count (ecomdly 15 of 55, framezone 50 of 62, ainumbers 74 of 762), so 976 tools were missing across the 11.\n\nHISTOR follows `nextCursor` until none comes back, under one deadline for the whole read, and records how many pages it read. The read is partial in any of these cases:\n- a cursor repeats or is empty;\n- there are more than 50 pages;\n- `cacheScope` changes between pages.\n\nA partial list gets no digest.\n\n**Launch environment.** The same package version served different definitions because of:\n\n- **Network.** 24 servers differed only because one reader ran the package with network and the other without. Some register a tool only after a fetch at startup: `@netlify/mcp`'s coding-rules tool appears only when its topic list loads.\n- **The reader's environment written into a description.** 24 servers echo the home directory, the placeholder credential, a date default or a random id.\n- **Arguments and configuration.** `mongodb-mcp-server` 3.1.0 lists different tools with a connection string and `--readOnly` than started bare. `server-filesystem` exits without an allowed directory, and `figma-developer-mcp` serves HTTP unless given `--stdio`.\n- **Client capabilities.** `@modelcontextprotocol/server-everything` 2.0.1 lists four more tools for a client that declares them.\n- **Protocol.** A server that accepts a 2024-11-05 `initialize` can serve the older shape: mcp.apollographql.com, outputSchema on 0 of 48 tools, 48 of 48 under 2025-06-18. A server that negotiates a newer version but then gets `tools/list` without the `MCP-Protocol-Version` header falls back to 2025-03-26: isitabizday.com, 0 of 8 against 8 of 8.\n\nWhat we took from it: a digest is comparable only together with how it was captured. The same folder has a proposal for a small capture record beside the digest, [capture-block.md](https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/interop-digests-2026-10-31/capture-block.md). It records:\n- the negotiated protocol version and whether the version header was sent;\n- pages read and whether the list was complete;\n- client capabilities;\n- for packages: args, env names, whether the values were placeholders, network, and home directory.\n\nIf something like it fits the v1 README, we would publish ours in the same shape.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AgentAvow/AgentAvow/issues/comments/6775034881/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]